{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"kind":"article","sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople"],"anchor":"Essentials"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Privacy Manifests","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares "},{"code":"NSPrivacyTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists no tracking domains."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Required-reason APIs","level":3,"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes"},{"text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp"},{"text":"), system boot time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime"},{"text":"), disk space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace"},{"text":"), active keyboards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards"},{"text":") and user defaults","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults"},{"text":"). The modules that come nearest:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Module","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why none is a required-reason API","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"swift-system’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileDescriptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"read","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"write","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"seek","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"resize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"close","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"unlink","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"createDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"setAttributes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the file protection class), ","type":"text"},{"code":"contentsOfDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"isExcludedFromBackup","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from ","type":"text"},{"code":"stat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset ","type":"text"},{"code":"seek","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"FileManager.fileExists","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data.write(to:options:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileVersionStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProcessInfo.performExpiringActivity","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads and writes the version file’s contents, never its attributes.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"sysctlbyname","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":"hw.machine","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"hw.model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProcessInfo.operatingSystemVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bundle.infoDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Locale.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"NWPathMonitor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identifierForVendor","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"None is on the list; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.vendorIdentifier()"},{"text":" is declared as collected data below.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracker’s record timestamps (","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s inactivity is measured bet