 hold (Product Interaction for taps and views, Purchase History for an order, and so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your identifiers."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" An identifier your app adds with an enricher of its own, such as an account","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier, is a User ID, linked to the user (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Your destinations.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Where your destinations send records decides whether the data leaves the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device, and whether a third party receives it. If an endpoint you send to uses the data for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracking, your app’s manifest lists its domain under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyTrackingDomains"},{"type":"text","text":", and your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asks for permission through App Tracking Transparency first."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Modules you turn off."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" If your app links a module but never turns it on, it collects nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through it, and your privacy labels can leave that data out."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"references":{"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","type":"topic","title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentrackin